Package: liblir-mqtt0.2
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: MQTT codec and topic grammar of the Lir message broker
 Lir is a clustered publish/subscribe bus that presents itself to clients
 as one MQTT broker, a hosted system on Dannan, the network layer.
 .
 This package holds lir::mqtt, the shared library every MQTT speaker in
 the stack links: the control packets of MQTT 3.1, 3.1.1 and 5.0 and the
 codec between them and bytes, and the grammar of topic names, filters
 and shared subscriptions. Patch releases of one minor keep its ABI, so
 the package is named for major.minor.

Package: liblir-client0.2
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: MQTT client library of the Lir message broker
 Lir is a clustered publish/subscribe bus that presents itself to clients
 as one MQTT broker, a hosted system on Dannan, the network layer.
 .
 This package holds lir::client, the small MQTT client the stack's
 projects publish and subscribe with: MQTT 5.0 or 3.1.1 over TCP or TLS,
 a password asked at every connect, QoS 0 and 1, a will, wildcard
 subscriptions kept across reconnects, and Lir's nodes found in Dannan's
 roster. Patch releases of one minor keep its ABI, so the package is named
 for major.minor.

Package: liblir-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends:
 liblir-mqtt0.2 (= ${binary:Version}),
 liblir-client0.2 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libboost-dev (>= 1.83),
 libdannan-dev (>= 0.10.2),
 libdannan-dev (<< 0.11~),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: MQTT codec and client of the Lir message broker (development files)
 Lir is a clustered publish/subscribe bus that presents itself to clients
 as one MQTT broker, a hosted system on Dannan, the network layer.
 .
 This package holds the headers and the CMake package configuration:
 find_package(lir <version> CONFIG), then link lir::mqtt or lir::client,
 which bring Dannan.
